  "id": "DrugBank_DB00874 - MONDO_5709",
  "verbalization": "Guaifenesin, a mucolytic agent, is implicated in the treatment of rhinitis, which in turn is associated with the common cold. The evidence suggests that Guaifenesin may serve as a bridge between rhinitis and the common cold through shared pathways involving the indication of rhinitis and its downstream effects. The presence of multiple indirect pathways—such as Guaifenesin → Rhinitis → Dextromethorphan or Pentoxyverine—indicates that the common cold may be influenced by the pharmacological effects of Guaifenesin via rhinitis, which is a common comorbidity in cold patients. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of Guaifenesin in modulating rhinitis, which could contribute to the development or resolution of the common cold. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Guaifenesin and the common cold through the rhinitis-indication chain, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
